MEETING TABLE
============

Purpose
-------
Represents one planned meetup or event.

Fields
------
- Id: Generated integer primary key
- Title: String
- Description: String
- Created at: Date/time when the host creates the meeting (storage type TBD)
- Host: User.Id (foreign key)
- Venue name: TEXT, required
- Venue city: TEXT, required
- Venue street address: TEXT, required; visible only to users with approved RSVPs
- Venue time zone: Required time-zone identifier (exact format and storage type TBD)
- Category: Exactly one category describing the kind or purpose of the event; MVP labels are Social/Conversation, Sports/Athletics, Business/Networking, and Hobbies. The list is fixed for the MVP; changes require an app update.
- Maximum group capacity: Integer, from 4 to 10 people total, including the host
- Interests: Interest[] (TypeScript app model; stored through MeetingInterest records)
- Start date and time: When the meeting begins, shown in the venue's local time zone (storage type TBD)
- RSVP cutoff date and time: Exact time chosen by the host; must be before the start time and shown in the venue's local time zone (storage type TBD)
- Status: Scheduled, Cancelled, or Completed (storage type TBD)

Relationships
-------------
- Each meeting has one host; a user can host multiple meetings.
- Non-host users request to attend through RSVP records.
- A meeting can have multiple interests; the connections are stored through MeetingInterest records.

Event lifecycle
---------------
1. A curated host creates and publishes the meeting; it becomes visible immediately. The meeting must be scheduled within 30 days of its creation.
2. Non-host users submit RSVP requests. The host approves or declines requests.
3. Approved RSVPs count toward the maximum capacity; pending requests do not. Once capacity is reached, new requests are no longer accepted.
4. The host chooses an exact RSVP cutoff date and time before the meeting; show it in the venue's local time zone.
5. At the cutoff, if fewer than four total participants (host plus approved RSVPs) are confirmed, the meeting is canceled or rescheduled and RSVP users are notified.
6. After the meeting, the host marks only the approved attendees who showed up; other approved attendees remain unmarked.

Additional decisions
--------------------
- If the host revokes an approved RSVP, the spot becomes available for another request.
- Rescheduling updates the same meeting; existing approved RSVPs stay active and attendees are notified.
- A rescheduled meeting remains Scheduled.
- Attendance may help measure participation and repeat attendance, but is not a safety rating.
- "Casual" is treated separately from category for now; how to represent event style is TBD.
- Transferring the host role may be considered as a future feature.
